+## Item 7 — new-bypass hunt
+
+1. BLOCKER — recursive credential screen admits a credential-shaped Authorization value that does not begin `Bearer `, `Basic `, `sk-`, or `sk_`.
+
+- Evidence: reproduced through the production checker CLI. A scratch evidence copy with a non-empty opaque `extra_headers.Authorization` value returned rc 0 PASS; a Token-scheme Authorization value also returned rc 0 PASS. No credential value is reported here. The recursive walker recognises the `Authorization` key only if `is_credential_name` sees one of its underscore/hyphen-separated segments; `AUTHORIZATION` is not in `CREDENTIAL_SEGMENTS`, while its value screen admits these non-prefix values (`C:170-190`, `C:676-693`).
+- Contract mapping: V-O2-2 freezes `Authorization` as a credential field anywhere below the provider block. The stated closure requires a nested credential under `Authorization` be caught; an arbitrary opaque credential value under that identity-bearing header is exactly that class.
+- Canonical path: PASS through `check_bundle` -> `check_transport` -> `_walk_credentials`, current PIN. This is not an in-process surrogate.
+- Material effect: a profile with a live credential value supplied via Authorization can be attested as key-free and satisfy the transport proof.
+- Discriminator: `/home/rocco/venv-agent-factory/bin/python ../scratch/o3_attack.py`; output `credential-authorization-opaque-value rc=0 ... PASS` and `credential-authorization-token-scheme rc=0 ... PASS`. Corrected implementation must rc 1 with a named dotted-path credential failure; the existing `Bearer` control stays red and clean profile stays positive.
+- Suggested fix: treat the `Authorization` header name case-insensitively as credential-bearing regardless of its value scheme; preserve `extra_headers` dotted path in the named rejection. Add opaque and `Token`-scheme regression tests beside `T:423-470`.
